From: Biscuit port <none@example.com>
Date: Sun, 17 Aug 2026 16:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mt8163-stp: expose WMT Wi-Fi function control at runtime

Stock enables the WMT Wi-Fi function as part of bringing Wi-Fi up, immediately
before the WLAN firmware download. This driver enables it during Bluetooth
bootstrap at t~1.77 s, and the WLAN driver then downloads and starts anywhere
from t~16 s to t~60 s - tens of seconds with the function enabled and nothing
driving it. Pulling stock's WMT userspace (6620_wmt_concurrency, 6620_launcher)
confirmed the rest of the split is already correct: WMT powers the chip,
downloads the ROM patch and toggles functions, and the WLAN driver downloads
its own firmware. The enable timing is the difference that is left.

Expose the function-control command as a write-only module parameter so it can
be toggled off and on again immediately before the WLAN driver is loaded,
reproducing stock's ordering without a cross-driver call and without a new
kernel command line per experiment.
---
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_mt8163_stp.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_mt8163_stp.c
@@ -1020,6 +1020,44 @@
  * Writable and read at probe, so it can be toggled by unbinding and rebinding
  * soc:bluetooth rather than by rebooting with a different command line.
  */
+/*
+ * Set to 0 or 1 to disable or enable the WMT Wi-Fi function at runtime.
+ *
+ * Stock issues this immediately before the WLAN firmware download; we issue it
+ * during BT bootstrap, tens of seconds earlier. Toggling it off and on again
+ * just before loading the WLAN driver reproduces stock's ordering without a
+ * cross-driver call.
+ */
+static struct mt8163_stp *stp_for_param;
+
+static int wifi_func_set(const char *val, const struct kernel_param *kp)
+{
+	static const u8 off_cmd[] = { 0x01, 0x06, 0x02, 0x00, 0x03, 0x00 };
+	struct mt8163_stp *stp = stp_for_param;
+	bool on;
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = kstrtobool(val, &on);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	if (!stp)
+		return -ENODEV;
+
+	ret = mt8163_stp_wmt_xfer(stp, on ? wmt_wifi_on_cmd : off_cmd,
+				  on ? sizeof(wmt_wifi_on_cmd) : sizeof(off_cmd),
+				  wmt_wifi_on_evt, sizeof(wmt_wifi_on_evt));
+	dev_info(stp->dev, "WMT Wi-Fi function %s -> %d\n",
+		 on ? "enable" : "disable", ret);
+	return ret ? ret : 0;
+}
+
+static const struct kernel_param_ops wifi_func_ops = {
+	.set = wifi_func_set,
+};
+module_param_cb(wifi_func, &wifi_func_ops, NULL, 0200);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(wifi_func,
+		 "write 1/0 to enable/disable the WMT Wi-Fi function now");
+
 static bool skip_ilm_patch;
 module_param(skip_ilm_patch, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(skip_ilm_patch,
@@ -1293,6 +1331,7 @@
 			 ret);
 	else
 		dev_info(stp->dev, "WMT Wi-Fi function enabled\n");
+	stp_for_param = stp;
 
 	dev_info(stp->dev, "WMT/STP bootstrap complete\n");
 	return 0;
